<%#
  The brand half of the sign-in and sign-up screens.

  Dark on purpose. Navy is in the palette but had no surface of its own, and
  the magenta and aqua only reach full strength against it -- on the near-white
  ground they have to be dropped to tints. It also gives the form half of the
  screen something to sit against.

  The canvas behind this is decoration and nothing depends on it: it is
  aria-hidden, it carries no content, and when it fails to load the gradient
  underneath is already the finished panel.
%>
<aside data-controller="brand-scene"
       class="brand-sky relative hidden flex-col justify-between overflow-hidden px-12 py-14 lg:flex">

  <canvas data-brand-scene-target="canvas"
          aria-hidden="true"
          class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 block h-full w-full"></canvas>

  <%# Darkens the left edge where the words are, without flattening the scene. %>
  <div aria-hidden="true" class="brand-sky-veil pointer-events-none absolute inset-0"></div>

  <div class="relative">
    <%= render "shared/wordmark", classes: "text-2xl", tone: :light %>
  </div>

  <div class="auth-enter-2 relative max-w-md">
    <h2 class="font-display text-5xl leading-[1.08] font-normal text-white">
      Every post.<br />
      Every story.<br />
      <%# Pink Lavender, the sign-in palette's one accent -- 7.3:1 on the
          Space Cadet ground. Decorative-adjacent but it passes as text. %>
      <em class="text-[#CEB5D4]">Stronger brand.</em>
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-6 text-base text-white/75">
      Manage your content, plan with ease, and grow your brand &mdash; beautifully.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="auth-enter-3 relative max-w-xs rounded-card border border-white/15 bg-white/[0.07] p-6 backdrop-blur-sm">
    <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-lg text-accent">&#10022;</span>
    <p class="mt-2 font-display text-lg text-white">All your brand, beautifully managed.</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-white/70">
      Plan content, engage your audience, and track growth &mdash; all in one place.
    </p>
  </div>
</aside>
